.TH "LE" "1" "Aug 2026" "le" ""

.SH NAME
le-wait - Block until a port frees up


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle wait PORT [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Block until PORT is free. With --timeout, give up after that long and
exit 124 — so a script can bound the wait instead of hanging, and can
tell a still-busy port from a le that couldn't run.

.PP
Exit codes: 0 success · 1 failure · 2 usage error · 124 --timeout elapsed.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for wait

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--timeout\fP=0s
	give up after this long (e.g. 30s); 0 waits forever


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBle(1)\fP


